        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Remove partial_implementation from ariaNotify() for Chromium]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30571</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30571"/>
        <updated>2026-09-18T10:50:36.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1152698?u=5ce323090a48b425ec70128365c96809699959f7&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Per discussion in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4387259215" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29610" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29610/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29610">#29610</a>, the unreliable announcement behaviour on macOS is a VoiceOver/OS limitation rather than a browser difference.</p>
<p dir="auto">I'm therefore removing the <code class="notranslate">partial_implementation</code> flag for Chromium, and rewriting the notes for clarity.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">This was tested by <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/janewman/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/janewman">@janewman</a>, who found nearly identical behaviour in Chromium and Firefox, and discussed with <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/caugner/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/caugner">@caugner</a> and <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/ddbeck/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/ddbeck">@ddbeck</a>.</p>
